(6138862, 902192, 5885, '<td valign="top">Greetings from Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Let me introduce myself. My name is Leroy Dickson, I''m a professional photographer, specializing in glamour, fashion and nude photography. But, I enjoy all forms of photography and appreciate the artistic efforts of all.<br/> <br/>First Impression:<br/>It''s a nice image of the quality I''d expect to see in a child''s book on animals. It''s well executed and pleasing to the eye.<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>When I first pulled up the image, I noticed that it was just a bit over-exposed. Not only does this make the image a bit brighter than I''d expect but also robs the color of its vibrance and saturation. If this had not been a min. ed. challenge, these could have been easily corrected in post. But, since it was limited to "out of the camera", exposure has to be dead-on. <br/> <br/>Otherwise the image is technically sound with nice focus and DoF.<br/> <br/>Artistic:<br/>It''s pleasing with a nice composition, can''t say I''d change a thing.<br/> <br/>How to grow its vote:<br/>DPC is big on the "Wow Factor" as you may know. Here, we often take for granted a photo that is pleasant to view. Had you shot the animal from a wierd point of view with a wide angle lens, voters probably would have gone nuts over it. However, IMO, the image would have been a less usable image for you. <br/> <br/>In closing:<br/> <br/>Nice image and a very good image for a stock photo portfolio. Definitely keep up the good work.</td>', 'Greetings from Critique Club: Let me introduce myself. My name is Leroy Dickson, I''m a professional photographer, specializing in glamour, fashion and nude photography. But, I enjoy all forms of photography and appreciate the artistic efforts of all. First Impression:It''s a nice image of the quality I''d expect to see in a child''s book on animals. It''s well executed and pleasing to the eye. Technicals:When I first pulled up the image, I noticed that it was just a bit over-exposed. Not only does this make the image a bit brighter than I''d expect but also robs the color of its vibrance and saturation. If this had not been a min. ed. challenge, these could have been easily corrected in post. But, since it was limited to "out of the camera", exposure has to be dead-on.  Otherwise the image is technically sound with nice focus and DoF. Artistic:It''s pleasing with a nice composition, can''t say I''d change a thing. How to grow its vote:DPC is big on the "Wow Factor" as you may know. Here, we often take for granted a photo that is pleasant to view. Had you shot the animal from a wierd point of view with a wide angle lens, voters probably would have gone nuts over it. However, IMO, the image would have been a less usable image for you.  In closing: Nice image and a very good image for a stock photo portfolio. Definitely keep up the good work.', '2010-08-23 16:48:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6138899, 902537, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from Critique Club:</b> <br/> <br/>Let me introduce myself. My name is Leroy Dickson, I''m a professional photographer, specializing in glamour, fashion and nude photography. But, I enjoy all forms of photography and appreciate the artistic efforts of all.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression:</b> <br/>A stunning, well-executed image of the Sn Fran bay. It''s a very nice image, worthy of a good stock photo portfolio.<br/> <br/><b>Technicals:</b> <br/>Technically the image is good, from exposure to focus. I don''t see any glaring errors.<br/> <br/><b>Artistic:</b> <br/>Compositionally, the photo is kind of weak. Only the top horizon placed on the third line draws my eye. Moving the horizon down to the bottom third and including more sky may have been a stronger composition. <br/> <br/><b>How to grow its vote:</b> <br/>Ehhh... as you may know, DPC is all about the "Wow Factor". Although this is a nice image, there''s nothing to make the viewer say wow, look at that... or how''d they do that. <br/> <br/><b>In closing:</b> <br/>I like the image. I personally think it should have placed higher, but I''m not the majority of the voters on the site. However, I encourage you to keep up the good work and I really enjoyed reviewing your image.</td>', 'Greetings from Critique Club:  Let me introduce myself. My name is Leroy Dickson, I''m a professional photographer, specializing in glamour, fashion and nude photography. But, I enjoy all forms of photography and appreciate the artistic efforts of all. First Impression: A stunning, well-executed image of the Sn Fran bay. It''s a very nice image, worthy of a good stock photo portfolio. Technicals: Technically the image is good, from exposure to focus. I don''t see any glaring errors. Artistic: Compositionally, the photo is kind of weak. Only the top horizon placed on the third line draws my eye. Moving the horizon down to the bottom third and including more sky may have been a stronger composition.  How to grow its vote: Ehhh... as you may know, DPC is all about the "Wow Factor". Although this is a nice image, there''s nothing to make the viewer say wow, look at that... or how''d they do that.  In closing: I like the image. I personally think it should have placed higher, but I''m not the majority of the voters on the site. However, I encourage you to keep up the good work and I really enjoyed reviewing your image.', '2010-08-23 17:43:05.000000', NULL, 0),
